# Direct toolchain dependencies for this project's CI workflows.
#
# The mbt packages are pinned to __MBT_REF__ - the mbt release tag that
# scaffolded this project, or the exact commit when it was a development build -
# which is reproducible and installable from a fresh checkout without a private
# index. A tag is MOVABLE though, on GitHub included, so the immutable form is
# the commit SHA - swap a tag for the SHA it points at when that matters.
#
# The block below pins the numerics stack at the exact versions the mbt install
# that scaffolded this project was running. Pinning mbt alone pins none of them,
# and they are the versions that decide model numerics: a floating training
# environment changes env_freeze_digest whenever any of them releases, which is
# the exact condition ADR-19 exists to detect. Renovate keeps them moving on
# purpose, one reviewed PR at a time.
#
# mbt-adapter-base is listed although nothing here imports it: every other mbt
# package depends on it, it is not on PyPI either, and pip can only satisfy
# that dependency from a ref it was given. Drop it and the install fails with
# "No matching distribution found for mbt-adapter-base".
#
# Once mbt is on PyPI, switch the four git refs to plain version pins and
# regenerate the fully transitive, hash-verified lock:
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt
mbt-adapter-base @ git+https://github.com/satrijandi/mbt@__MBT_REF__#subdirectory=packages/mbt-adapter-base
mbt-core @ git+https://github.com/satrijandi/mbt@__MBT_REF__#subdirectory=packages/mbt-core
mbt-xgboost @ git+https://github.com/satrijandi/mbt@__MBT_REF__#subdirectory=packages/mbt-xgboost
mbt-mlflow @ git+https://github.com/satrijandi/mbt@__MBT_REF__#subdirectory=packages/mbt-mlflow
__PINNED_DEPS__
